  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag569" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;KPC PIPELINE, LLC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 11pt;"&gt;December 31, 2024 and 2023&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE A - THE KPC PIPELINE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Nature of Business&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The KPC Pipeline is a 1,000 mile interstate pipeline owned by KPC Pipeline, LLC (&amp;#8220;KPC&amp;#8221; or the &amp;#8220;Company&amp;#8221;).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC is engaged in interstate transportation of natural gas and is subject to the rules, regulations, and accounting of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;) pursuant to the Natural Gas Act and certain other statutes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC is a wholly owned subsidiary of MV Pipelines, LLC (&amp;#8220;MV Pipelines&amp;#8221;).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 4.75pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;#8220;GAAP&amp;#8221;).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The accompanying financial statements include a provision for federal and state income taxes since these taxes are a cost component in rates allowed by the FERC. This provision for income taxes is not reflected in KPC&amp;#8217;s separate financial statements prepared in accordance with GAAP.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC&amp;#8217;s accounting policies generally conform to Accounting Standards Codification Topic 980 (&amp;#8220;FASB ASC 980&amp;#8221;) &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic;"&gt;Accounting for the Effects of Certain Types of Regulation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;. The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) the classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of operations, and statement of cash flows, and (2) under FASB ASC 980 certain assets and liabilities from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt; -aw-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The preparation of KPC&amp;#8217;s financial statements in accordance with FERC requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities, the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities that exist at the date of the financial statements, and revenues, costs, and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;3.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Cash&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;In June 2013, KPC filed a cash management plan under which the owner of MV Pipelines provides cash management services to KPC in accordance with the FERC Order No. 634-A.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '4'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;4.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Accounts Receivable&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC is exposed to credit losses primarily through sales of natural gas transportation services. Credit risk relates to the risk of loss that the Company could incur as a result of non-performance by counterparties pursuant to the terms of their contractual obligations. To reduce credit risk, KPC monitors its ongoing credit exposure through active review of counterparty balances against contract terms and due dates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC estimates expected credit losses on accounts receivable using a loss rate method. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The loss rate is derived from historical experience with adjustments for current economic conditions, and forward-looking information. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Under the loss rate method, a historical loss rate is applied to the outstanding accounts receivable balance to determine the allowance for credit losses. Additionally, KPC periodically reviews accounts receivable balances for collectability, and allowances are established for customer specific amounts considered uncollectible.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, KPC did not have an allowance for credit losses and incurred no credit loss expense for the years then ended.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '5'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC extends credit to its customers for transporting natural gas through its interstate natural gas pipeline. The concentrations of customers may affect KPC&amp;#8217;s overall credit risk in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic, regulatory, and other factors.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;See Note J for additional information.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '6'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;6.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Transportation and Exchange Gas Balances&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;In the course of providing transportation services to customers, natural gas pipelines may have differences between natural gas delivered on to the pipeline and natural gas delivered off of the pipeline.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;These transactions result in transportation and exchange gas imbalance receivables and payables.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Such imbalances are recorded as current assets or current liabilities in the accompanying balance sheets using the posted index prices of the applicable approved tariffs, which approximate market rates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;These imbalances are required to be resolved within a specified period of time and the resolution can be through imbalance trading with other shippers or by utilizing the cash-out procedures specified in each tariff.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '7'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;7.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Additions to utility plant are recorded in the property accounts at cost.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;For constructed assets, these costs include contracted services, materials and indirect charges for engineering, supervision and general and administrative costs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Expenditures for maintenance and repairs are charged to operations as incurred.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Expenditures for renewals and betterments, which materially extend the useful lives of assets or increase their productivity, are capitalized.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Gains or losses on retirements that include an entire depreciable property unit are included in operations.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;All other dispositions or retirements are removed from property accounts at cost and such amounts plus removal costs less salvage are charged to accumulated depreciation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Annual depreciation is computed using the straight line method based on economic or FERC mandated lives as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 605.25pt; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;

&lt;tr style="height: 15pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 18.5pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 449pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;Main line system&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 136.25pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;2.50%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 15pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 18.5pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 449pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;Pumping equipment, buildings and tanks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 136.25pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;5.00% - 10.00%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 17.25pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 18.5pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 449pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;Compressors, meters and other operating equipment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 136.25pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;2.5% - 20.00%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 16.5pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 18.5pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 449pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;General - vehicles, office furniture and equipment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 136.25pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;14.38% - 28.57%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '8'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt; -aw-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;8.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Asset Impairment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;An impairment loss is recognized when the carrying amount of a long-lived asset used in operations is not recoverable and exceeds its fair value.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The carrying amount of a long-lived asset is not recoverable if it exceeds the sum of the undiscounted cash flows expected to result from the use and eventual disposition of the asset.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;A long-lived asset is tested for recoverability whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that its carrying amount may not be recoverable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;If an impairment is determined to exist, KPC will request guidance from FERC as to the recording of any such impairment.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;No impairment loss was recognized for the years ended December 31, 2025 or 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '9'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 10.44pt; -aw-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;9.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;As a limited liability company, KPC is a disregarded entity for federal income tax purposes. All items of taxable income and expense pass through to the members of MV Pipelines.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;For regulatory purposes, KPC accounts for income taxes based on an asset and liability approach.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Under this approach, deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized based on future tax consequences attributable to differences between financial statement carrying amounts of assets and liabilities and their respective tax basis.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Deferred tax assets and liabilities are measured using enacted tax rates in effect for the year in which those temporary differences are expected to be recovered or settled.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;In accordance with KPC&amp;#8217;s rate order (RP99-485-000), which was approved by the FERC in September 2002, KPC set its net tax basis for FERC reporting purposes equal to its net book basis at the date of acquisition by Enbridge Midcoast Energy, L.P. in November 1999.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The current tax liability recognized each year in accordance with FERC requirements will be relieved through proprietary capital in the subsequent period as a capital contribution (see Note F).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '10'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;10.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;While the FERC has not adopted FASB&amp;#8217;s revenue recognition guidance and disclosure requirements (ASC 606 &amp;#8211; Revenue from Contracts with Customers), there remains no difference between the revenue recognized under GAAP and FERC due to the application of the right to invoice practical expedient. In the application of the right to invoice practical expedient, the Company&amp;#8217;s revenues from regulated capacity arrangements are recognized based on rates specified in the contract or the Company&amp;#8217;s FERC tariff. Therefore, the amount invoiced, which includes the capacity contracted and variable volume of natural gas transported, corresponds directly to the value the customer received. These revenues are recognized monthly once the Company&amp;#8217;s performance obligation to provide capacity has been satisfied. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company disaggregates revenues from contracts with customers by contract type; however, effectively all the Company&amp;#8217;s revenues were from capacity arrangements and transportation contracts with customers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company transports natural gas on behalf of customers from contractually-agreed-upon receipt points to contractually agreed-upon delivery points.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company recognizes reservation fees related to fixed transportation contracts in the period for which volumes were reserved.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company recognizes revenue related to interruptible transport volumes at the time of receipt.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Revenue related to park and loan services is recognized pro-ratably over the term of the contract.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Natural gas transmission revenues are recognized net of costs. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company does not disclose the value of unsatisfied performance obligations for (i) contracts with an original expected length of one year or less and (ii) contracts for which the variable consideration is allocated entirely to a wholly unsatisfied performance obligation, as allowed under ASC 606. Under the Company&amp;#8217;s contracts, each MMBtu of natural gas represents a separate performance obligation; therefore, future volumes are wholly unsatisfied, and disclosure of the transaction price allocated to remaining performance obligations is not required.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '11'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;11.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Allocation of Salary and Overhead Expense Policy&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Certain payroll, insurance, interest, and office expenses are allocated to KPC using a direct allocation method.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;See Note N for additional information.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '12'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;12.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Fair Value of Financial Instruments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The carrying amounts of receivables, accounts payable, and accrued expenses approximate fair value due to the short-term maturity or highly liquid nature of those instruments. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '13'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;13.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Effective January 1, 2003, KPC adopted Order No. 631, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic;"&gt;&amp;#8220;Accounting, Financial Reporting, and Rate Filing Requirements for Asset Retirement Obligations&amp;#8221;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt; (&amp;#8220;Order No. 631&amp;#8221;), which addresses accounting and reporting for asset retirement obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived tangible assets. Order No. 631 requires entities to record the fair value of a liability for the retirement obligation in the period in which the liability is incurred if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. The associated asset retirement costs are capitalized as part of the carrying value of the asset, which is subsequently depreciated over its useful life. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC is permitted to include annual charges for cost of removal in its regulated cost of service rates charged to customers. The amounts charged to customers for the costs related to the retirement of the long-lived tangible assets differ from the period costs for depreciation of the asset retirement obligation (&amp;#8220;ARO&amp;#8221;) asset and accretion of the ARO liability recognized in accordance with Order No. 631. Therefore, this results in a difference in the timing of recognition of period costs for financial reporting and rate-making purposes. Because the requirements of FASB ASC 980 are met, KPC recognizes a regulatory asset or liability for differences in the timing of recognition of the period costs associated with asset retirement obligations for financial reporting and rate-making purposes (See Note H).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '14'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;14.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Recently Issued Accounting Pronouncements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;In January 2023, the Company adopted ASU No. 2016-13, Financial Instruments - Credit Losses (Topic 326) Measurement of Credit Losses on Financial Instruments. In Docket No. AI20-2-000 released by FERC on May 7, 2020, the current expected credit losses (&amp;#8220;CECL&amp;#8221;) method is a reasonable methodology and is acceptable for FERC financial accounting and reporting purposes. The CECL model utilizes a lifetime expected credit loss measurement objective for the recognition of credit losses for financial instruments at the time the financial asset is originated or acquired. The expected credit losses are adjusted each period for changes in expected lifetime credit losses. This model replaced the multiple existing impairment models in current GAAP, which generally required that a loss be incurred before it is recognized. The adoption of this guidance did not have a material impact on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '15'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.28pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;15.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.28pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC has evaluated activity from December 31, 2025 through April 8, 2026, the date the financial statements were available to be issued. No subsequent events were identified which would require recognition or disclosure in the financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8.65pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 11pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8.65pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 11pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE C - PROPERTY, PLANT AND EQUIPMENT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Property, plant and equipment consisted of the following at December 31:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
