&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE I - OTHER REGULATORY LIABILITIES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;At December 31, 2025 and 2024, a regulatory liability of $2,552,964 and $2,584,452, respectively&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;, is recorded as a deferred credit for the difference in timing between the cumulative period costs for depreciation of the ARO asset and accretion of the ARO liability associated with the asset retirement obligation for financial reporting purposes and the cumulative amount collected through the rate making process for the asset retirement obligation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE J - MAJOR CUSTOMERS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Operating revenues consist of transportation revenues relating to customers in the states of Kansas and Oklahoma.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Kansas Gas Service, a Division of ONEOK, Inc. (&amp;#8220;KGS&amp;#8221;) and Atmos Energy Corporation (&amp;#8220;Atmos&amp;#8221;) accounted for approximately 75% and 10%, respectively, of revenues in 2025. KGS and Atmos accounted for approximately 77% and 11%, respectively, of the revenues in 2024.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE K - OPERATING LEASES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;On December 27, 2018, the FERC issued guidance for the accounting and financial reporting for leases (Docket No AI19-1-000). The guidance addressed how to apply the FERC&amp;#8217;s accounting and reporting requirements related to lease arrangements in response to GAAP&amp;#8217;s ASC 842. Under the FERC&amp;#8217;s accounting regulations, operating leases are not required to be capitalized and reported in the balance sheet accounts established for capital leases. However, the FERC will permit jurisdictional entities to record operating leases that may be capitalized under ASC 842 in the FERC balance sheet accounts that have already been established for capital leases assets and liabilities if certain tracking, reporting and internal controls are in place.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;All other provisions of the FERC&amp;#8217;s accounting and reporting requirements for lease accounting were not affected by ASC 842.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;ASC 842 has no impact on the existing ratemaking treatment or practices.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC elected not to capitalize its operating leases and continues to follow the Commission&amp;#8217;s accounting regulations for operating lease accounting. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;KPC has non-cancelable leases for office, warehouse space and office equipment. These future minimum rental payments under all non-cancelable leases at December 31, 2025 were as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
