&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;At December 31, 2025 and 2024, capital assets of $10,783 and $294 are held in accounts payable, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;In addition, the Company&amp;#8217;s parent converted a receivable from the Company (which represents the Company&amp;#8217;s prior year current income tax provision) into proprietary capital of $578,880 and $533,812 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;Furthermore, during the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company received a capital distribution from its investment in associated companies totaling $1,754,892. This transaction resulted in a reduction to both the investment in associated companies balance and proprietary capital.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE N -&lt;/font&gt; &lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; font-weight: bold;"&gt;RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;As discussed in Note B3, affiliated companies provided cash management services to the Company during 2025. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the amount of cash held by these affiliated companies on behalf of the Company was $0.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;As discussed in Note B11, certain expenses are allocated to the Company by affiliated companies. Allocated charges totaled $4,432,561 and $3,360,128 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. If KPC were a stand-alone entity, operating expenses could potentially differ from the amounts presented due to differences in cost structures and the absence of shared services. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Garamond;"&gt;The Company is listed as a co-borrower on a credit facility of an affiliated company. Although the Company had no borrowings under the facility, the Company&amp;#8217;s assets serve as collateral for the credit facility.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
